      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is a pretty neat feature, but, it is, of course, one of the things VRChat uses for partnerships Sanrio Vfest and  VKet. \nIf it was publicly available, there's some security and privacy concerns around this that go beyond what is already possible with things like @{5f8a26770aaa28611fedd6b6|full_name}'s analytics using (IIRC!) GAS+google drive as described below, of course, and you brought that up. \nVRChat does however allow you to \"out of the box\" link social media accounts and youtube videos to to your vrchat profile and world ids. It would be nifty to have access to some of those \"safe\" API linked accounts like twitter and other social media be something accessible from udon and the quick menu perhaps. \nIt's also possible some of that stuff is planned for vrchat's internal creator monetization program in the future, but I have no idea. That makes sense to me.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-11-15T16:44:12.299Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Requesting that we could put web \"links\" in worlds that open a web browser window to a specified URL.\nPossible uses include:\n-Linking to the creator's personal website\n-Linking to rules documents for complex games\n-Linking to polls or surveys\nOf course it would be bad to just open a web browser window so perhaps these URLs could be handled similar to how video player URLs are. I also suggest some kind of popup when you click a link, asking for your permission to open a web window (See image for photoshopped mockup).\nI think it would be nice for creators and useful for users. Seems like a more convenient version of putting a QR code in your world (which can't easily be scanned in VR).",
